  "cautions": [
    "A positive descriptive B gain is NOT a statistical test of stable behavioral identity until source-day constrained permutation null / tag-accuracy negative controls and month-independent re-exposure are fitted",
    "Steps, animal-days and individual-month reuse same foxes; 10 months are not ten independent ecological studies",
    "Different site-year cohorts have population density, habitat, anthropogenic-food and management differences already described in original source article; no causal site comparison",
    "Spatial grid and clock bins do not guarantee identical micro-habitat, individual task, sex or prey availability",
    "Movement speed mode from GPS may contain individual tag/collar noise and duty-cycle artifacts; HDOP and satellite gating do not remove all GPS measurement confounds",
    "No resource E, temporal encounter T, or competition outcome independently obtained",
    "Original source animal IDs and GPS positions not exported; field data analyzed in memory only"
  ],
  "interpretation": "Source fox individuals show positive conditional out-of-day movement-mode predictive gain in multiple spatially shared site-year months, but effect sizes vary, can approach 0 or turn negative and are not null-calibrated. This is a potentially biological within-shared-place pattern to independently test, not proof of stable individual niche specialization."
